::ENG2_U05_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence corrects the convention error in "students cannot focus good"?{
=A. Students cannot focus well.#Correct. Well is the correct adverb to describe how students focus.
~B. Students cannot focus good.#Incorrect. Good is the wrong form here.
~C. Students cannot good focus.#Incorrect. The word order is unclear.
~D. Students good cannot focus.#Incorrect. This is not standard English.
}

::ENG2_U05_L08_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.V.02] Which pair shows a word and its derivation?{
~A. loud and quiet#Incorrect. These are related by contrast, not derivation.
=B. revise and revision#Correct. Revision is derived from revise.
~C. school and hallway#Incorrect. These are related by topic, not derivation.
~D. good and awesome#Incorrect. These are similar in meaning, not a derivation pair.
}

::ENG2_U05_L08_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.V.03] In a formal proposal, why is "awesome" usually weaker than "beneficial"?{
~A. Awesome is always negative.#Incorrect. Awesome is positive, but it is informal.
~B. Beneficial means the opposite of helpful.#Incorrect. Beneficial means helpful or producing a good result.
=C. Awesome has a casual connotation, while beneficial sounds formal and precise.#Correct. The connotation of beneficial better fits a formal audience.
~D. Awesome is a convention error.#Incorrect. The issue is tone, not grammar.
}

::ENG2_U05_L08_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best fits school leaders as the audience?{
~A. This change would be awesome for kids.#Incorrect. The wording is informal and vague.
~B. It is nice because people need it.#Incorrect. This is vague and unclear.
~C. The library should do stuff after school.#Incorrect. This is informal and imprecise.
=D. Extended library hours would support students who need a supervised place to complete assignments after school.#Correct. This revision is precise, formal, and audience-aware.
}

::ENG2_U05_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] What is the main purpose of the synthesis draft in Lesson 8?{
~A. To tell a personal story about a favorite library book.#Incorrect. The draft is not a personal narrative.
=B. To explain why a supervised after-school study space would help students.#Correct. The draft focuses on supporting students who need a study space after school.
~C. To compare two poems about libraries.#Incorrect. The draft is not literary comparison.
~D. To define every vocabulary word in Unit 5.#Incorrect. Vocabulary helps the revision, but the draft's purpose is not a definition list.
}
